    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] The park contains a drainage divide separating the West Savanna River, which drains to the Mississippi River and the Gulf of Mexico, from the East Savanna River, which flows in an opposite direction to the Saint Louis River, Lake Superior and the Great Lakes, and the Saint Lawrence River to the Atlantic Ocean.\n[2] The furthest north and west of the Great Lakes chain, Superior has the highest elevation and drains into the St. Mary's River.\n[3] The Saint Louis River (abbreviated St. Louis River) is a river in the U.S. states of Minnesota and Wisconsin that flows into Lake Superior.\n[4] A small strait connects it to the Saint Louis Bay to the west, into which the Saint Louis River empties."
